 "notes": "Cut the ~70-item bullion coin list to the major programmes as archetypes with metal and redesign versions; 18 secondary national programmes kept in m. Dropped as minor wildlife/sovereign-licence issues: Frigatebird (Antigua), Noah's Ark (Armenia), Barbados Trident, Bhutan Lunar, Cambodia Lost Tiger, Cameroon Mandrill, Giraffe (Equatorial Guinea), African Leopard (Ghana), Lady Justice (Gibraltar), Iranian Emami, Snow Leopard (Kazakhstan), Tiger (Laos), New Zealand Kiwi, Taku Turtle, Birds of Paradise, African Ounce (Rwanda), Nikola Tesla (Serbia), HMS Bounty, World's Wildlife (DR Congo), Isle of Man Cat, Silverback Gorilla, Tokelau sea creatures, South Sea Dragon, Spanish Iberian Lynx, Dragon Rectangular Coin, Melita, Mexican Onza Troy. Gold Sovereign left to the Circulation coin archetype (00_00); Gold Swan kept as m. Kept old apmex kind sources. Silver Eagle Stacker and Intaglio rounds stay as m/r: no retrieved page describing them."
